Another thing worth mentioning is that the application service is responsible for translating
primitive types, such as string or decimal, to value objects. The edge always uses
serializable types that have no dependencies on the domain model. The application service,
however, operates with domain concerns; it needs to tell our domain model what to do,
and since our domain model prefers to receive data as value objects, the application service
is then responsible for the conversion.
The code for handling commands for an existing entity looks very similar to handling
updates for existing entities. In fact, only the line where we call the entity method is
different. Therefore, we can significantly simplify the Handle method by using a
