Protecting the internal state from being invalid and, as a result, bringing the model into an
inconsistent state, is one of the most important characteristics of aggregates. Aggregate
invariants must be satisfied for each operation that triggers a state change; thus, we need to
ensure that we control the aggregate state when calling any command method on the
aggregate.
Let's look at what complex rules we have for our classified ad entity. To find such rules, we
