3, EventStorming, and put them on a chart, as follows:
Business rules can prevent the command execution
Analyzing constraints for a command
We put the command to the left side, the event to the right side, and try to find out what
could prevent our command from being executed in a way that it produces the desired
outcome (the event). In our case here, we need to ensure that before an ad can be put to the
review queue, it must have a non-empty title, text, and price.
Consistency Boundary Chapter 7
[ 195 ]
We cannot put these checks combined with the value object, since before the ad is sent to
review, it can have an empty title and text, and it can have no price. Only when a given
command is being executed do we need to check whether these constraints are satisfied. It
is what we can call an invariant for this entity — an ad that is in a pending review cannot
have an empty title, empty text, or zero price.
There are at least two ways of ensuring that our entity never gets to an invalid state. The
first and most obvious way is to add checks to the operation code. There is no way of
requesting that the ad be published, so let's add it and make some changes related to the
fact of using value objects for the entity state as well:
