Here, we have renamed the _events collection to _changes to make the naming more
explicit. We also added a call to EnsureValidState to the Apply method. This means that
whenever we execute an operation that is supposed to change the aggregate root entity
state, we apply a new event and the state changes in the When method. However, before
adding the new event to the list of changes, we check whether the new state is valid and
that no invariants are broken. If the new state violates the invariants, we throw an
exception.
