In order to implement memento, we need to have a way to convert our complex object to
something that can be persisted, like a text file, relational table, or JSON object. Upon any
save operation, we'd need to manually convert the state of our aggregate to the memento,
and when we retrieved the state back, a reverse operation would be required. However,
today, we can solve this issue by telling Entity Framework Core that we are, in fact, dealing
with value objects, and not work entities. In fact, the EF Core has implemented all of the
pieces of the pattern for us. To use this feature, we need to add more code to the
